 "findings": [
  {
   "evidence": "The proof at lines 387-392 is exactly that normalization: `refine (hasDerivAt_sphericalBesselJ (l + 1) x).congr_deriv ?_; have hl : (l + 1 : \u2115) - 1 = l := by omega; have h2 : (l : \u2115) + 1 + 1 = l + 2 := by omega; simp only [hl, h2]; push_cast; ring`. Grep for `sphericalBesselJ_succ` across `code/` shows uses only inside the file's own docstring and the derived `deriv_sphericalBesselJ_succ`. Mathlib keeps no successor variant of `hasDerivAt_pow` either (`Mathlib/Analysis/Calculus/Deriv/Pow.lean:137` is the only form), so there is no upstream precedent for the duplicate shape.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Mathematics/SpecialFunctions/SphericalBessel/Basic.lean",
   "fix": "Delete both and use `hasDerivAt_sphericalBesselJ (l + 1) x` / `deriv_sphericalBesselJ (l + 1) x` (with `push_cast` where the `\u2191(l+1)` form is inconvenient); drop their entry from the module docstring main-statements list (line 77).",
   "issue": "`hasDerivAt_sphericalBesselJ_succ` (line 383) and `deriv_sphericalBesselJ_succ` (line 396) are `hasDerivAt_sphericalBesselJ`/`deriv_sphericalBesselJ` at order `l + 1` with nothing changed but `Nat.cast_succ`: `(l+1)-1` reduces to `l` and `x ^ (l+1+1)` to `x ^ (l+2)` definitionally, and both forms are stated in the same `sphericalBesselJDivPow` vocabulary, so the successor pair carries no content the general pair lacks. Neither is used anywhere in the repo.",
   "line": 383
  }
 ],
